# Trivy allowlist for the Phase 2 security gate (scripts/ci/scan.sh --ignorefile).
#
# Policy — an entry here is an accepted risk, so it must be reviewable:
#   • one advisory ID per line (CVE-YYYY-NNNNN or GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx);
#     package globs and wildcards are rejected by tests/test_ci_hygiene.py
#   • each entry gets a preceding comment with: why, owner, and the date to re-check
#   • the gate ignores findings with no released fix (--ignore-unfixed) instead of
#     pretending they are absent, so this list only ever holds *fixable* items we
#     consciously defer
#
# Typical legitimate entries look like this (all currently empty on purpose —
# Phase 1 ships with no accepted vulnerabilities):
#
#   # CVE-2024-XXXXX — libexpat: XML external entity, unreachable (we never parse
#   #   untrusted XML). Owner: platform. Re-check at the next python:3.12-slim bump.
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX
#
# Trivy also reads .trivyignore inside each scan target and supports
# --ignorefile per-scan, so a service can hold a narrower exception if it ever
# needs one. Prefer bumping the base image over editing this file.
